      "content": "okay, so if policy is the main accelerant, then wouldn't it be more accurate to say that the inequality isn't just a \"side effect\" of the economy, but actually a direct result of how the system is currently designed? like, if the rules are written to favor capital over labor, isn't that a deliberate choice by the people in power?",
